  "raw_label": "appellant_won",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "S. Subbaiya vs The Commissioner on 5 December, 2024 Author: G.K.Ilanthiraiyan Bench: G.K.Ilanthiraiyan W.P Before The Madurai Bench Of Madras High Court Dated: 05.12.2024 Coram The Honourable Mr. Justice G.K.Ilanthiraiyan W.P (MD).No.29221 of 2024 S. Subbaiya . Vs. 1. The Commissioner Tamil Nadu Food Safety and Drug Administration, Dms Campus, 5th Floor, No. 359, Annasalai, Teynampet, Chennai - 6. 2. The Designated Officer Tamil Nadu Food Safety and Drug Administration Department, Food Safety Wing, Sivagangai District. 3. The District Collector Collectorate, Sivagangai District. 4. The Superintendent of Police Office of the District Superintendent of Police, Collectorate, Sivagangai District. 5. The Sub Inspector of Police Aaravayal Police Station, Devakottai Taluk, Sivagangai District. ... Respond Prayer: Petition filed under Article 226 of the Constitution o issue a Writ of Mandamus directing the respondents herein to remove the and seal put on the petitioner shop at Aaravayal Village, Devakottai Tal https://www.mhc.tn.gov.in/judis 1/4 W.P S. Subbaiya vs The Commissioner on 5 December, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/70257494/ 1 Sivagangai District forthwith by considering petitioner's representation 12.11.2024. For Petitioner : Mr.R.Paranjothi for M/s.KBS Law Office For Respondents : Mr.D.Gandhi Raj Special Government Pleader for R1 : Mrs.M.Aasha Government Advocate (Crl.Side) f ORDER Therefore, an F.I.R has been registered as against the petitioner in Crime No.91 of 2024 for the offence under Section 24(1) of C i g a r e t t e a n d o t h e r T o b a c c o P r o d u c t s A c t , 2 0 0 3 . S u b s e q u e n t l y , t h e https://www.mhc.tn.gov.in/judis 5. The Sub Inspector of Police Aaravayal Police Station, Devakottai Taluk, Sivagangai District.",
    "facts": "While being so, the fifth respondent conducted inspection and found that the petitioner is selling Cigarette and other tobacco products, without any licence. petitioner admitted his guilty and he paid fine. Thereafter, the second respondent came to the petitioner's shop and lock the petitioner's tea stall premises by putting seal and also affixed the order dated 30.10.2024. 4. On perusal of the order dated 30.10.2024, it revealed that the petitioner's licence was cancelled temporarily until further orders.",
    "arguments": ""
  },
